WEBVTT

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.200
Do you have your grandfather's Bright Stone?

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.150
I do. Why do I have to always carry it?

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.590
You'll figure that out if you 
listen carefully at the church.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:27.300
<i>What's my dad talking about?</i>

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.300
<i>If only Squeak could talk, too.</i>

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:51.030
<i>Dad said that Mommy made Squeak.</i>

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:57.180
<i>If he could talk, would he tell me things?</i>

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.330
Squeak?

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.330
Wait! Squeak!

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:41.880
Oh, my...

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:48.000
Well, isn't this a rare thing?

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.610
Welcome, little lady,

00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:00.630
to the town of Alloween,
the world of dreams and illusions!

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.230
<b>The Apathetic Boy and the Girl in a Bottle</b>

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:36.400
<b>The Lord with You in Dreams and the Town of Oblivion (Part 1)</b>

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:39.220
We're almost ready to go, jamo!

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:44.490
We're not going to the country near here?

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.920
Yeah, that's the country of the dead, jamo.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:51.670
At this time of year, it'll be 
hard to sell anything there, jamo.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.600
Really?

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:56.620
What's wrong, Toto?

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:58.970
Jamo?

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:01.090
Where are you going?

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:04.260
Don't go off on your own. It's dangerous!

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.350
Jeez...

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:14.910
What's gotten into you, Toto?

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:19.620
It's kinda cold.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:25.450
What was that?

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.880
A g-g-ghost!

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.040
Seriously?

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.350
Don't tell me you're afraid of ghosts.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:33.760
Of course not—

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:37.060
And you got scared too, Merc!

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:42.340
When you were a kid, if you read a 
ghost story, you couldn't sleep!

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.220
The fog's getting thicker.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.360
Be careful.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:52.400
I'm not sure what we can do about it.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:12.080
Is this the country of the dead?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:15.440
There are so many people. It feels so alive.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:18.260
Now what, Toto?

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:23.000
Your name's Toto, huh?

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:28.580
If you have a monster with you,
does that mean you're from the outside?

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:30.190
Yeah, I guess.

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:34.040
We're traveling around the world 
with Jamo-san, a merchant.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:37.780
I'm jealous. I want to go on a journey, too.

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:41.640
I think about it every time I look 
at the paintings in the mansion.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:44.770
Um... Well...

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:45.110
I always thought I wanted to see 
the sights in them for myself.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:46.820
Oh, sorry.

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:53.320
It's been so long since 
I've talked to anybody.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.840
Are you from this town?

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:01.070
Today's the Bright Stone Festival.

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:03.130
Bright Stone?

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:07.340
Everybody in this country carries 
a special stone with them

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:10.590
from the day they're born 
till the day they die.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.580
And that's the Bright Stone?

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:18.570
When they die, their soul leaves their body 
and goes to dwell in the Bright Stone.

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:23.820
And what's that got to do 
with the festival today?

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:27.150
During the Bright Stone Festival, 
those that cared about you

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.150
will destroy your Bright Stone 
so that your soul can move on.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.950
If you don't destroy their stone,

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:36.700
the people you love won't
 be able to rest in peace.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:42.030
They'll be stuck in this world forever.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:48.240
So the festival today is very 
important to the people here.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:52.310
Yeah. It's the most important 
event in this country.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:55.370
Thanks for telling us.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:56.410
It's fine.

00:06:57.690 --> 00:06:59.860
Yuu-san, what's wrong?

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:01.860
Nothing.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:03.770
And so...

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:07.940
I want to ask your help with something.

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:14.440
I want you to give this to a friend of 
mine who lives in a castle on the hill.

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:21.680
Uh, no, I'm not blaming you.

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:24.330
I understand that Eleanor is...

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:25.910
Um...

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:28.430
But it's been eight years.

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:31.290
If you keep holding on to her Bright Stone,

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:36.440
she'll be stuck here in this world forever.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.650
Luciano...

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:41.730
I'm grateful to you.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:45.700
Cosette's love for picture books 
is due to your influence.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.320
But...

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.740
Well, whatever.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.590
Look, Cosette seems lonely...

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:55.770
Cosette?

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:01.580
Did you see a girl with a stuffed animal?

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:04.120
I think she went that way.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:07.590
But the cursed castle is that way!

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:10.770
Don't take it seriously.

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:12.390
It's "cursed," but...

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:13.560
You look around here!

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:15.520
Wait!

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:22.880
Where am I?

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:24.470
The town of dreams.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:26.530
Dreams?

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:28.400
What dreams?

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.380
That's your choice to make,

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:34.060
and also mine.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.790
Who are you?

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:42.290
Do you mean to tell me you 
know exactly who you are?

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:44.550
I'm Cosette.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:46.920
No, no.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.300
I mean, what are you?

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:52.880
You don't have a pumpkin 
head like me, do you?

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:57.200
I live in Leib Village.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.470
And my dad...

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:02.250
And I belong to my mom and dad?

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:04.350
Hmm...

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:08.360
You don't know who you are, do you?

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.830
You don't, either?

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:13.830
A moment here is a day.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.620
A day is a year.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:18.780
And a year is a moment.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:23.070
It's not surprising you 
would forget who you are.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:27.060
What's important is where you are,

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:29.520
and where you want to go.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.270
Where...?

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.360
Correct.

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:38.100
Or perhaps, what you want.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.670
You should have something like that, too.

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:44.590
This is the town of dreams.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:49.100
Everything you want can be yours!

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:54.690
I don't get it.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:58.900
Then I'll show you around!

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:01.270
Leave it to me.

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:08.540
Now, hold on tight...

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.040
One...

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:11.050
Two...

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:12.930
Three!

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:20.620
I'm not falling?

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.600
This is the town of dreams.

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:30.680
If you wish it, you can 
walk through the sky,

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:33.360
or even create a path of stars.

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:44.350
Everybody's always wondered about what 
fantastic worlds sleep within them.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:48.470
My name is Shtoruiyu.

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:53.340
Call me Mister Shtoruiyu!

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:58.760
<b>The Apathetic Boy and the Girl in a Bottle</b>

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.740
I've never walked through the sky before.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.530
You're amazing, Mister!

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:30.780
You'll be able to do it 
without my help soon.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:32.870
Like this?

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:37.490
Wonderful!

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:40.260
You have the power to dream real dreams!

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:45.020
You can become the princess of this world!

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:48.030
Will you be the king, then?

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.360
That sounds nice.

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:52.150
Huh?

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:53.360
What?

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:57.350
I feel something echoing in my empty head.

00:11:58.060 --> 00:11:59.150
Look! On your head!

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:02.310
Yay! Yay!

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:04.600
Oh, you?

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:07.720
Stop slamming into my head.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:09.910
It echoes.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:11.640
Sorry, Mister!

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:13.770
Hello there, girlie!

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:15.220
Bye!

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.670
Wh-Who was that?

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:20.850
The residents of the town.

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:24.660
Many dreams mix here.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:27.610
Sometimes another's dreams 
can get lost here.

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:30.930
Is your dream here, too?

00:12:33.530 --> 00:12:35.200
Perhaps it is.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:37.650
When you're here for so long,

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:42.070
you forget which dreams are yours,
 and which ones aren't.

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:48.920
But even my empty pumpkin head

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:52.840
remembers that there was something I sought.

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:58.120
Will that happen to me someday?

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:01.380
Nobody knows.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:02.740
But...

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:08.530
Everything you wish for is here.

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:21.440
Squeak!

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:22.860
A rat?

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:25.170
Just kidding.

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:27.000
Who's there?

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:31.280
Jeez... Did you even forget that?

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:33.160
Look down.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.450
Down here!

00:13:38.470 --> 00:13:42.590
Hey, don't tell me you've forgotten my face.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:45.740
I'm the most handsome rat in the land.

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:46.960
And my name is...

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:48.650
Squeak.

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:51.590
Hey there, partner.

00:13:51.590 --> 00:13:54.790
You look pretty glum.

00:13:55.090 --> 00:13:57.140
Am I dreaming?

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:59.720
You can't be here. It's impossible.

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:00.950
Dreaming?

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:04.940
Nobody but her knows.

00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:09.060
You're a fantasy that only exists within me.

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:12.440
Yeah, you get it.

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:14.880
Come on, chin up.

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.620
Welcome, partner,

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:27.760
to the town of Alloween,
the world of dreams and illusions!

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:33.980
Hello?

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:38.760
This place is creepy.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:42.210
Creepy?

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:44.270
Give me!

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:47.540
There they are!

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:49.690
Ghosts!

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:56.450
What do we do?

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:57.750
What should we do?

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:03.480
Run away!

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:05.200
H-Hey!

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:06.490
Wait!

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:08.060
After them!

00:15:10.190 --> 00:15:14.070
You can have everything here.

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:15.850
Be anyone!

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:19.330
Thank you.

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:27.180
But that doesn't mean much if 
I don't even know what I want.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:30.890
What's important is what you want!

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:37.870
I've looked for years for something 
to fill my empty pumpkin head.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:42.900
I've looked for all kinds of 
fun and beautiful dreams.

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:50.700
But those dreams never stay within my head.

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:55.230
They leave without making a sound.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:58.340
But things have changed since I met you.

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:02.950
Every time I speak about my dreams with you,
 something echoes in my head,

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:06.530
and it's not the sound of empty 
pumpkins slamming together!

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:11.270
Together with you, I may 
be able to find my dream,

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:14.480
and make new dreams!

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:18.120
Cosette, you and I together...

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:21.380
Were you always alone?

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:25.870
It feels like I was always alone,

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:28.170
but it also feels like I wasn't.

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:31.840
The dream I wish for,

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:37.090
left behind beyond a moment, a month, 
a year, or perhaps an eternity...

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:40.600
I think I understand you.

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:44.440
Then would you stay here and live with me?

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:48.760
I'm tired of searching for 
dreams I'll never find.

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:51.560
You are a fragment of my dreams.

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:53.950
A seed that will someday become a dream.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:56.440
A spring from which dreams are born.

00:16:58.060 --> 00:16:59.820
Please, Cosette.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.570
Don't leave me alone.

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:07.140
What's with the spaced-out look?

00:17:07.140 --> 00:17:10.000
You want me to give you a stab 
with my favorite sword here?

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.850
Yeah, just enough to wake me up.

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:16.490
Okay, here I go.

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:19.090
Ow!

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:21.590
Aren't you a stuffed animal?

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:24.640
That's just how it works in reality.

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:28.400
Here, I'm a powerful warrior rat,

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:32.660
who's survived many battles 
with his partner.

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:39.380
And this rapier is a legendary blade that 
pierces everything and never fails!

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:42.970
That's the story, right?

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:45.270
Yeah.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.190
I don't like being alone, either.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:55.050
But when I talk to you, it feels 
like I've forgotten something.

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:58.670
Maybe it's like when you lock your door,

00:17:58.670 --> 00:18:02.810
but get worried and go back to check later.

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:09.300
Maybe I already had what I sought.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:13.720
So your answer is no, then, miss?

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:19.330
If someday, I can't handle 
being alone, just like you...

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:23.170
I'll tell you "yes," then.

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:28.220
For now, I want to look 
for the thing I seek.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:31.000
I've just arrived here.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.760
And I've still only just met you.

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:38.880
Search for it before you forget 
the warmth in your hands.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:44.060
The heart is so vast that you'll 
get lost without a guide.

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:49.380
I've been lost a long, long time.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:52.130
When I was a child,

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:57.030
before I went to bed, I went 
on many adventures with you.

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:58.000
Yeah.

00:18:59.510 --> 00:19:03.430
We defeated fire-breathing dragons 
and flew through the sky in magic shoes.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:08.120
We challenged a golem to 
attain the legendary rapier

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.280
and swam through a sea of stars.

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:14.590
You and me were famous. We never lost.

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:19.240
But it was all in my imagination.

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:20.560
It wasn't real.

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:23.760
The legendary rapier, the sea of stars...

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.350
And you, too?

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:34.600
When did that...

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:36.700
I told you.

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:40.110
This is the town of dreams 
and illusions, Alloween.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:43.120
I'm a product of your imagination, 
so if I'm talking,

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:48.290
singing, or flying through the sky,
there's nothing unusual about that at all.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:51.540
Why am I here?!

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:54.780
That's your decision to make, partner.

00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:58.710
If you're here, it means 
you're seeking something.

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:01.100
That's how dreams work.

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:04.800
Well, the only things I'm seeking 
are a partner I can count on

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:07.300
and the kiss of a princess.

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:09.390
That's right.

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:10.720
Look!

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:11.990
Help me!

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:12.650
I'm scared!

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:14.020
Run!

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:18.240
Tell me this, partner.

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:21.090
Who's been captured by the evil dragon?

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:22.740
The kind princess.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:24.120
That's right.

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:27.650
Come on, partner.
 Let's go on another adventure.

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:29.420
Yeah.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:31.380
Let's go.

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:38.750
Why do we have to run so much?

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:41.220
We'll lose sight of Toto!

00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:50.090
Merc? Toto?

00:20:53.570 --> 00:20:54.730
Huh?

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:57.650
Where did they go?

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:59.150
Jeez...

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:01.100
Sorry!

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:03.280
What is this?

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:09.370
Pictures of the family who lived here?

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:12.260
This child...

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:21.920
My house?

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:41.250
I'm back.

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:45.570
Yuu, Dad's home.

00:21:49.090 --> 00:21:50.540
Welcome back!

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:53.220
Yeah, glad to be home.

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.060
It's me, Titi!

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:28.070
It's me, Chacha!

00:23:28.070 --> 00:23:29.980
My head's spinning round and round!

00:23:29.980 --> 00:23:32.120
This is a different <i>Merc StoriA</i> than usual!

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:32.690
Yeah!

00:23:32.690 --> 00:23:35.270
Don't forget to bring your pot lid!

00:23:35.270 --> 00:23:38.340
Next time: "The Lord With You In 
Dreams and the Town of Oblivion."

